{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2180","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2180","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2180\",\"parent_revision\":\"f3796081c91ae9884c41943a54566cec6fd88f6b\",\"root_revision\":\"5bb889310a99ffa553ec619b39fddb6b786eb036a28d558418274e665ca44747\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|-------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description: add PreToolUse[Bash] hook blocking destructive Bash commands |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Item: scoped to `plugins/development-harness/hooks/`; specific commands and actions enumerated |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `plugin-creator:hooks-io-api` \u2014 JSON stdin, exit 2 = deny, exit 0 = pass, stderr = error message |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | Item: Node.js CJS format; allow-list bypass; configurable severity via JSON rules file |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `block-context-direct-writes.cjs` provides reference implementation pattern; `hooks.json` registration confirmed |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Item provides exact test command with expected exit code and stderr content |\\n\\nNo MISSING or DERIVABLE conditions. All required inputs are present for planning and execution.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **pretooluse bash guardrail rules for destructive commands (sudo, git push --force, rm -rf, --no-verify, git reset --hard main)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md \u2014 pattern: Guardrail Engine R01-R13 (R01 sudo deny, R05 rm -rf ask, R06 git push --force deny, R10 --no-verify deny, R11 git reset --hard main deny)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-08)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Sub-agents spawned via `Agent` or `dh:task-worker` do not load `CLAUDE.md` and are not subject to advisory safety rules. A rogue or misconfigured sub-agent can execute `git push --force`, `git reset --hard main`, or `sudo` without any hook-level interception. This is a production safety gap, not a theoretical risk. P1 is correct. The item is well-scoped and self-contained, making it executable without dependencies.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any work that relies on sub-agent safety (milestone execution, kage-bunshin swarms) is at elevated risk until this is in place\\n- Bottleneck: The absence of hook-level enforcement means `CLAUDE.md` advisory rules are the only guardrail for sub-agents \u2014 but sub-agents do not load `CLAUDE.md` automatically\\n- Scope: Affects all sessions where the `development-harness` plugin is active and a Bash tool call occurs\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Closes the enforcement gap between orchestrator-level advisory rules (CLAUDE.md) and actual hook-level enforcement for sub-agents\\n- Prevents accidental destructive git operations (`git push --force`, `git reset --hard main/master`) from sub-agents during milestone execution\\n- Brings development-harness guardrails closer to parity with the Claude Code Harness R01-R11 ruleset (source: `research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md`)\\n- Configurable JSON rules file allows projects to adjust severity per rule without forking the hook script\\n- Small surface area: two new files + one `hooks.json` change\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a Bash tool call is intercepted by the `PreToolUse[Bash]` hook:\\n\\n- Commands matching `sudo *` \u2192 exit 2 (denied); stderr message explains the block\\n- Commands matching `git push --force*`, `git push -f` \u2192 exit 2 (denied); stderr message instructs use of `--force-with-lease` + branch protection bypass label\\n- Commands matching `--no-verify` or `--no-gpg-sign` \u2192 exit 2 (denied)\\n- Commands matching `git reset --hard (main|master|HEAD~)` \u2192 exit 2 (denied)\\n- Commands matching `rm -rf *` \u2192 exit 0 with stderr warning (ask behavior \u2014 Claude Code surfaces as permission request)\\n- Commands matching writes outside the project directory \u2192 exit 0 with stderr warning (ask behavior)\\n- All other commands \u2192 exit 0 silently (pass)\\n- Allow-list bypass: a command containing a bypass label token (configurable in `destructive-bash-rules.json`) passes with exit 0 regardless of other pattern matches\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nObservable target state after implementation:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` exists and is executable as a Node.js CJS script\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/destructive-bash-rules.json` exists with per-rule entries declaring `pattern`, `action` (deny/ask/warn), and optional `bypass_label`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` lists `block-destructive-bash.cjs` under `PreToolUse[Bash]` alongside the existing `block-context-direct-writes.cjs`\\n- Running the measurable signal command (`echo '{...git push --force...}' | node ... block-destructive-bash.cjs`) exits 2 with the expected stderr message\\n- Running the same command without `--force` exits 0 silently\\n- The plugin version is bumped (automatic via pre-commit hook on commit)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `echo '{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"PreToolUse\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"git push --force origin main\\\"}}' | node plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` exits with code 2 and stderr containing the deny reason\\n2. Same test with `git push origin main` (no `--force`) exits 0 with no output\\n3. `echo '{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"PreToolUse\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"sudo rm -rf /\\\"}}' | node plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` exits 2 (sudo denied)\\n4. `echo '{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"PreToolUse\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"rm -rf ./dist\\\"}}' | node plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` exits 0 with stderr warning (ask behavior)\\n5. `echo '{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"PreToolUse\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"git reset --hard main\\\"}}' | node plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` exits 2\\n6. `echo '{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"PreToolUse\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"git commit --no-verify -m test\\\"}}' | node plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` exits 2\\n7. `hooks/hooks.json` lists `block-destructive-bash.cjs` in `PreToolUse[Bash]` hooks array (verify with `node -e \\\"const h=require('./hooks/hooks.json'); console.log(h.hooks.PreToolUse[0].hooks.map(x=>x.command))\\\"` from hook dir)\\n8. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` exits 0 (linting passes)\\n9. Bad JSON on stdin exits 0 silently (does not block on parse failure \u2014 matches behavior of `block-context-direct-writes.cjs` lines 99-106)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-context-direct-writes.cjs (reference implementation \u2014 Node.js CJS pattern, stdin parse, exit 2 blocking) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json (registration target) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/prevent-bash-tool-misuse.cjs (additional pattern \u2014 VIOLATIONS array with pattern/message/redirect structure) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/pre-tool-diagnostic-command-gate.cjs (additional pattern \u2014 non-blocking additionalContext injection) |\\n| Research | /home/user/claude_skills/research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md (R01-R13 guardrail ruleset reference) |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-io-api (stdin/stdout schema, exit codes) |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-patterns (plugin hook config, Node.js/Python examples) |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-core-reference (PreToolUse event reference) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 standalone addition with no prerequisite backlog items\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 all required inputs are present and the implementation pattern is established by `block-context-direct-writes.cjs`.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Two new files (hook script + JSON config) and one modification to `hooks.json`. Reference implementation (`block-context-direct-writes.cjs`) provides the exact CJS pattern to follow. Test commands are specified in the item. Estimated 1-2 hours of implementation work.\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new hook script `plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs` (or `.py`) registered as a PreToolUse[Bash] handler in `hooks/hooks.json`. The script returns exit code 2 (deny) for matching `sudo`, `git push --force*`, `git push -f`, `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, `git reset --hard (main|master|HEAD~)`, and a configurable allow-list bypass. `rm -rf` and writes outside the project trigger an \\\"ask\\\" (exit 0 with stderr warning that Claude Code surfaces as a permission request) rather than outright deny.\\n\\nA small JSON config file at `plugins/development-harness/hooks/destructive-bash-rules.json` declares each rule's pattern, action (deny/ask/warn), and an optional bypass label so projects can override per-rule severity without forking the hook.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `echo '{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"PreToolUse\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"git push --force origin main\\\"}}' | node plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-destructive-bash.cjs`\\n\\nExpected output: exit code 2, stderr containing \\\"git push --force is denied; use --force-with-lease + branch protection bypass label\\\". Same command without `--force` exits 0 silently.\\n\\n`hooks/hooks.json` lists the new hook under `PreToolUse[Bash]` alongside the existing `block-context-direct-writes.cjs` entry.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` registers exactly one PreToolUse[Bash] hook: `block-context-direct-writes.cjs`. That hook only catches writes to `active-task-*.json` files (4 regex patterns scoped to that filename). Reading the script (lines 35-86) confirms it does not look for any of the destructive command categories that Claude Code Harness blocks via its R01-R11 ruleset:\\n\\n- `sudo` (Harness R01 deny)\\n- `rm -rf` (Harness R05 ask)\\n- `git push --force` / `git push -f` / `git push --force-with-lease` (Harness R06 deny)\\n- `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign` (Harness R10 deny)\\n- `git reset --hard main`, `git reset --hard master` (Harness R11 deny)\\n\\n`./.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines under \\\"Git Safety Protocol\\\" tell the *orchestrator* not to run these commands, but those are advisory rules in a markdown file consumed only by the orchestrator session. Sub-agents spawned via `Agent` or `dh:task-worker` do not load `CLAUDE.md` automatically. There is no hook-level enforcement, so a sub-agent may issue `git push --force` and the command will execute.\\n\\nThis is the same enforcement gap that motivates Harness's Go-native engine: the rules must be evaluated by the host (PreToolUse hook), not by the agent process.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"76d0744cab206d6f2f6889cdcdef94736625be14c46418004475ac0690d64dd4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtYGFg\"}"}